The pre-built map assets in `assets/*.bin.z` were derived from the
following sources, all of which are in the public domain. No license
restrictions apply to redistribution, but attribution is given here
out of good practice.

Earth day map (used to derive `earth_classes.bin.z`):
    NASA Visible Earth — Blue Marble: Land Surface, Ocean Color, Sea Ice
    and Atmosphere
    https://visibleearth.nasa.gov/collection/1484/blue-marble
    Public Domain (NASA imagery)

Earth specular / land-water mask (used to derive `earth_classes.bin.z`):
    Derived from a NASA Blue Marble bathymetry / specular reflection
    composite, mirrored by the Three.js project as
    https://threejs.org/examples/textures/planets/earth_specular_2048.jpg
    Public Domain (NASA imagery)

City lights (used to derive `earth_lights.bin.z`):
    NASA Earth Observatory — Black Marble: Earth at Night 2016
    https://earthobservatory.nasa.gov/features/NightLights
    Public Domain (NASA imagery)

Cloud cover (used to derive `earth_clouds.bin.z`):
    NASA MODIS / Visible Earth cloud fraction composite
    https://visibleearth.nasa.gov/collection/1484/blue-marble
    Public Domain (NASA imagery)

All four source images were retrieved through the Three.js texture
mirror at https://threejs.org/examples/textures/planets/ and converted
to the compact binary format used at compile time by `tools/build_assets.py`
(also under MIT, part of this repository).

Astronomical formulas:
    Subsolar point — simplified NOAA Solar Position Algorithm
    Moon orbit and phase — simplified Meeus Astronomical Algorithms,
    chapter on lunar position
